<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dome of Soltaniyeh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1313</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as mausoleum at Sultaniyya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dome of Soltaniyeh is the mausoleum of the Ilkhanid ruler Öljaitü at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultaniyya">Sultaniyya</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, completed around 1313. Its huge double-shelled brick dome is one of the great achievements of Persian architecture and a major monument of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>'s cultural legacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dome-of-soltaniyeh.jpg" alt="Dome of Soltaniyeh" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jb-mhr · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dome_of_Soltaniyeh_jb1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
